A||||15||Songman||Rare T-top on eBay???||||1||
Z||000000||Songman||07-16-2001||11:34 PM||||Did anyone happen to catch this one yet?<P>Here is how he opens his description...<BR>From 1984 through 1988, Pontiac only made 97 4-cylinder automatics with T-tops. These cars were sent from the factory to have the T-tops installed at a sub-contractor. There are very few of them left, and even fewer 1988 models, which make it a real collector's item.<P>Only 97! And ever rarer in 88! Dang! My car is rarer than I thought! I sometimes wonder where people get this informatation! And sometimes I also think people just make up anything to try to sell something.<P>It gets better too! It is the 3rd best Fiero in the Eastern US! It has to be. He won a 'stinkin' trophy with it at the Turkey Run...<P>I hope this isn't a forum members car cause I don't want to hurt anyone's feelings, but a little truth in advertising is in order here... It's not a bad looking little car, but sell it for what it is.<BR> <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=593403450&r=0&t=0" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/ebayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=593403450&r=0&t=0</A> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 07-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||DRH||07-16-2001||11:46 PM||||LOL, Did you miss this part?<P>"This car has the Tech 4 engine, not one of the problem-prone aluminum engines in earlier models"<P>Where can I get me one of dem dare 'luminum engines???||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||07-16-2001||11:49 PM||||Wait, now I'm confused...<P>Why then do they call those engines "Iron Dukes?"<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000003||Oreif||07-17-2001||12:24 AM||||What a crock! LOL! What get's me is that across the rear window it says:<BR>Central Florida Fiero's<BR>Assuming he is actually part of the club. If it's the "3rd best on the east coast" why didn't he take it to the big Fiero Show in Daytona earlier this year? (Maybe he did but he didn't win anything.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   )Although it is a T-Top, I think $3000 for an 88 coupe with an auto and A/c but no other options is a little high.<BR>The 2.5L are called "Iron Duke" because that is what Pontiac called them back in the late 70's when they first came out with them. (They replaced the Chevy 140cu.in. aluminum 4-cyl that came in Vega's) The "Tech IV" refers to the re-designed head that was used on the FWD version of the engine. There never has been an "Aluminum" Duke 2.5L. ||||reg||10
Z||000004||Raydar||07-17-2001||12:44 AM||||Kinda reminds me of that "rare" V-6 4-speed, I saw the other day.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Actually it *does* have kinda low miles. He might actually get his asking price. Maybe.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||12
Z||000005||AusFiero||07-17-2001||02:32 AM||||Hmmm like to know where he got his 84 stats into the equation. When I checked my t-top history with C&C (when still alive) they reckoned my t-tops was one of the earliest sets ever fitted and that was in 86 1/2.<P>Mind you I only spoke to an office type so who knows?<P>Of course the 88s are always going to be dearer with the factory option sticker that made them a true factory option (even though fitted by C&C) as apposed to a dealer option that could be fitted by anyone the dealer chose to do it.<P>Maybe he will get his price.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
